01:57:51.270 --> 01:57:52.103
Just really quickly.

01:57:52.103 --> 01:57:54.320
We didn't talk about
supplements much today.

01:57:54.320 --> 01:57:56.060
In the previous episodes I talked about

01:57:56.060 --> 01:57:58.650
the phosphocreatine system and
supplementing with creatine,

01:57:58.650 --> 01:58:00.020
I talked about beta alanine

01:58:00.020 --> 01:58:02.750
for kind of moderate duration work.

01:58:02.750 --> 01:58:05.661
You know really the only
things that have been shown

01:58:05.661 --> 01:58:10.661
to really improve endurance
work across the four varieties

01:58:11.880 --> 01:58:14.250
of endurance work I described today.

01:58:14.250 --> 01:58:16.550
They have essentially two forms.

01:58:16.550 --> 01:58:17.470
One, are stimulants.

01:58:17.470 --> 01:58:19.680
So things like caffeine will definitely

01:58:19.680 --> 01:58:22.320
improve endurance work and power output.

01:58:22.320 --> 01:58:23.500
There's a little bit of evidence

01:58:23.500 --> 01:58:26.130
that caffeine intake can actually inhibit

01:58:26.130 --> 01:58:27.720
the function of the creating system,

01:58:27.720 --> 01:58:30.220
but it's just one study.

01:58:30.220 --> 01:58:31.610
But that's interesting.

01:58:31.610 --> 01:58:32.580
If you want to read that study,

01:58:32.580 --> 01:58:35.430
you can put caffeine into www.examine.com

01:58:35.430 --> 01:58:37.410
and it will take you to that study.

01:58:37.410 --> 01:58:39.410
Many people get sore after workouts,

01:58:39.410 --> 01:58:40.500
in particular workouts

01:58:40.500 --> 01:58:42.570
that involve a lot of eccentric loading

01:58:43.560 --> 01:58:45.190
or workouts that are very novel

01:58:45.190 --> 01:58:48.690
where they've kind of pushed
it instead of moving gradually

01:58:48.690 --> 01:58:51.860
as I suggest into say high
intensity anaerobic endurance

01:58:51.860 --> 01:58:55.120
work of three sets of 20
seconds on 100 seconds rest.

01:58:55.120 --> 01:58:58.090
Maybe you get over ambitious
and you do eight sets.

01:58:58.090 --> 01:59:00.540
In which case you are extremely sore.

01:59:00.540 --> 01:59:02.340
Certain forms of magnesium in particular,

01:59:02.340 --> 01:59:05.280
magnesium malate, M-A-L-A-T-E.

01:59:05.280 --> 01:59:09.270
Have been shown to be useful for removing

01:59:09.270 --> 01:59:12.860
or reducing the amount of
delayed onset muscle soreness.

01:59:12.860 --> 01:59:14.960
That form of magnesium
is distinctly different

01:59:14.960 --> 01:59:16.410
than the sorts of magnesium that are good

01:59:16.410 --> 01:59:17.590
for getting us into sleep.

01:59:17.590 --> 01:59:20.000
Things like magnesium three
and eight and Bisglycinate.

01:59:20.000 --> 01:59:24.100
And then there's this whole
thing about beet powder

01:59:24.100 --> 01:59:28.260
and beet juices and things
that increase nitric oxide

01:59:28.260 --> 01:59:31.020
and allow for more vasodilation
and therefore delivery

01:59:31.020 --> 01:59:33.360
of blood to muscle and
neurons and other tissues

01:59:33.360 --> 01:59:34.990
for long bouts of endurance work.

01:59:34.990 --> 01:59:39.130
Some people like beet juice
and they related compounds

01:59:39.130 --> 01:59:41.260
that increase arginine and vasodilation.

01:59:41.260 --> 01:59:42.610
Some people don't.

01:59:42.610 --> 01:59:45.340
Some people don't feel
good when they take those.

01:59:45.340 --> 01:59:46.510
Some people also don't feel good

01:59:46.510 --> 01:59:47.870
when they take beta alanine,

01:59:47.870 --> 01:59:49.370
because it can give them this feeling

01:59:49.370 --> 01:59:52.720
of kind of like itchy, creepy
crawlies under the skin

01:59:52.720 --> 01:59:55.330
kind of the niacin
phenomenon, the niacin flush.

01:59:55.330 --> 01:59:56.360
Some people don't mind that,

01:59:56.360 --> 01:59:58.190
or some people don't experience that.

01:59:58.190 --> 01:59:59.420
So when it comes to supplementation

01:59:59.420 --> 02:00:00.340
there's a lot of variety.

02:00:00.340 --> 02:00:04.240
But magnesium malate has
been shown to reduce soreness

02:00:04.240 --> 02:00:05.660
as sometimes that's good.

02:00:05.660 --> 02:00:08.080
Cold and hot contrast therapy for soreness

02:00:08.080 --> 02:00:09.210
things of that sort.

02:00:09.210 --> 02:00:14.210
But in general, we focused
mainly today on behavioral tools.

02:00:14.220 --> 02:00:17.920
You'll notice that all of
the tools are accessible

02:00:17.920 --> 02:00:20.400
without the need for lots of equipment.

02:00:20.400 --> 02:00:21.600
So I didn't say you need a rower,

02:00:21.600 --> 02:00:23.900
or you need a kettlebell
though those will work.

02:00:23.900 --> 02:00:27.190
And I hope I was able to
illustrate for you that endurance

02:00:27.190 --> 02:00:28.260
isn't just one thing.

02:00:28.260 --> 02:00:32.480
It's not just the ability to
go for long bouts of exercise

02:00:32.480 --> 02:00:33.460
of different kinds,

02:00:33.460 --> 02:00:35.010
that there's also this mental component

02:00:35.010 --> 02:00:36.700
because of the way that neurons work.

02:00:36.700 --> 02:00:39.730
And also that there are these
different forms of endurance

02:00:39.730 --> 02:00:40.790
of muscular endurance,

02:00:40.790 --> 02:00:41.680
that where you're going to fail

02:00:41.680 --> 02:00:45.060
'cause of the muscles and
muscle energy utilization

02:00:45.060 --> 02:00:47.110
and the nerves that innovate
those muscles locally

02:00:47.110 --> 02:00:50.680
not because of a failure to
bring in oxygen or blood.

02:00:50.680 --> 02:00:52.140
Whereas long duration effort.

02:00:52.140 --> 02:00:53.970
It's going to be more about,

02:00:53.970 --> 02:00:55.587
you know, being below your VO2 max,

02:00:55.587 --> 02:00:58.060
and your ability to be
efficient for long bouts

02:00:58.060 --> 02:01:00.210
of more than 12 minutes of exercise.

02:01:00.210 --> 02:01:04.630
One set, as they say of 12
minutes to maybe several hours.

02:01:04.630 --> 02:01:07.210
I should just mention with
long duration type work.

02:01:07.210 --> 02:01:09.340
You know, you could even
imagine raking in the yard

02:01:09.340 --> 02:01:11.380
or mowing a lawn depending
on how big that lawn is.

